(wire (pts (xy 151.13 172.72) (xy 153.67 172.72)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid 59e959cd-a6bb-589e-861a-258c47922519))
(global_label "LED_K" (shape passive) (at 153.67 172.72 0) (fields_autoplaced) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 4b326b10-7454-517b-b69f-d2ac1908c971) (property "Intersheetrefs" "${INTERSHEET_REFS}" (at 153.67 172.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide)))
(text "Sheet 2: LED driver power stage. Boost, 100 kHz, gate from U7 (sheet 4) on PWM2. 12 LEDs in series, 35.4 V at 0.565 A = 20 W." (at 25.4 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid c39dda4b-3272-5c80-8fc0-9e841beae351))
(text "LED board (off-board, excluded from PCB): D4-D15 in series between J6 pin 1 (VLED) and J6 pin 2 (LED_K). NTC2 for the LED board is on sheet 3." (at 25.4 154.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 4d0d58ea-0459-5e93-8b21-8176b743a129))
(text "Notes\n- Q1: 60 V N-MOSFET, Rds(on) <= 10 mOhm, Qg <= 25 nC. L1: 100 uH, Isat >= 3.5 A, DCR <= 40 mOhm. F2: 5 A. These three have no footprint yet.\n- Q2: logic-level 60 V N-MOSFET, Rds(on) <= 20 mOhm at 4.5 V (SOT-23 footprint assumes G-S-D = 1-2-3; check the part).\n- F2 protects against a shorted LED string: a boost has a DC path from input to output.\n- Hot loop Q1 -> D1 -> C18/C19/C22/C23 -> R13 must be as small as possible.\n- R13 feeds only the over-current comparator (sheet 4). LED current is regulated in firmware from R14 through U6.\n- R14: Kelvin connect ILED_P and the R14 ground pad to U6 IN+ / IN-.\n- R5/R6: ADC reading of the LED voltage and the 43.3 V over-voltage trip.\n- Optional synchronous boost: Q6 (60 V, <=14 mOhm) across D1, gate from PWM3 through a second UCC27211; keep D1 for the dead time." (at 25.4 200.66 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 20d21805-ac7d-5406-98ca-2bb7d9473e71))
)
